167
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Tebîet gundê wadî, çiqas rind e.
 
Nature of such a village, how beautiful it is.

168
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:53,000
Seke... çiya, kelêm... çiya, kelêm, wane...
 
Look... mountain, rocks... mountain, rocks, those...

169
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Şîn e, pirr xweş e. Bêhna vazê tê çinîn.
 
Green, very nice. The smell of flowers comes to be picked.

170
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Xay, gundo xweş xay.
 
Oh, nice village oh.

171
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Wane... wane alîmin e.
 
Those... those are my side.

172
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Bêjer... mejer... naken gundo bijîn.
 
Say... they don't make the village live.

173
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Bes ye alîmî gundo jî nekanî li bêjer bijîn.
 
But the one of my side of the village also cannot live on
the...

174
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Dê, noka istim jêke, nikanim li bêjer bijîm. Xêr e, sebra
min hat. Ha elmim gundo.
 
So, now [unclear], I can't live on the [unclear]. It's good,
my patience came. I got used to the village.

175
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Gund pirr xweş e.
 
The village is very nice.

176
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Çoyî gewr bigre, berf se... pîdî ke.
 
Take the grey tea, snow... make it...

177
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Diyê, wî hewşê li ser banê hoo...
 
See, that courtyard on the roof hoo...

178
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Dê me ne bicoysî Orte.
 
Don't [unclear] us Middle.

179
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Holê!
 
Hello!

180
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Holê!
 
Hello!

181
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Kale ma yî tê?
 
Uncle, are you coming?

182
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Keremke, keremke.
 
Welcome, welcome.

183
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Silav aleikum.
 
Peace be upon you.

184
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Aleikum selam.
 
Upon you be peace.

185
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Tu çawayî baş î?
 
How are you, are you good?

186
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Ez kole te me, tu bi xêr hatî.
 
I am your servant, you are welcome.

187
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Tu bi xêr hatî ser çava.
 
You are welcome upon eyes.

188
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Tu bi xêr hatî.
 
You are welcome.

189
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Emrê te çiqas e xalo?
 
How old are you uncle?

190
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Welle emrê min ez nizanim.
 
Well, my age I don't know.

191
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Te leşkerî kiriye?
 
Have you done military service?

192
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Haaa, leşkerî min berê kiriye.
 
Haaa, military service I did long ago.

193
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Te berê kiriye?
 
You did it long ago?

194
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Haa, gelek çûye.
 
Haa, much time has gone.

195
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Maşalla.
 
Mashallah.

196
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,000
Ew kî ye?
 
Who is that?

197
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Ew jina min e.
 
That is my wife.

198
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Jina te ye?
 
Your wife?

199
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Xaltîkê...
 
Auntie...

200
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Merheba jêre.
 
Hello to him.

201
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Merheba, tu çawayî baş î?
 
Hello, how are you, are you good?

202
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Alêykum selam, hemû bi xêr hatin ser çavan.
 
Upon you be peace, all welcome upon eyes.

203
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Ser çava, spas dikim xaltîkê.
 
Upon eyes, thank you auntie.

204
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Ellah we bihêle.
 
May God keep you.

205
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Keremkin, keremkin.
 
Come in, come in.

206
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Wele karê me heye emê herin.
 
Really we have work, we will go.

207
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Wîî, na na, keremkin, qehwekî vexwin.
 
Oh, no no, come in, drink a coffee.

208
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Em hatin gundê we bibînin.
 
We came to see your village.

209
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Ser çavan hatin.
 
Came upon eyes.

210
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Ellah we bihêle.
 
May God keep you.

211
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Xwedê emrê we dirêj bike.
 
May God extend your life.

212
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Ellah razî be.
 
May God be pleased.

213
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Hûn pîr û kal bûne.
 
You have become old (woman) and old (man).

214
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Em pîr û kal bûne, em ketine.
 
We have become old, we have fallen/declined.

215
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Hûn ketine?
 
You have fallen?

216
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Em ketine, wele halê me nemaye.
 
We have fallen, really our strength hasn't remained.

217
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Maşalla, siheta xalê min pirr xweş e.
 
Mashallah, my uncle's health is very good.

218
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Sihet xweş e, şukur ji Xwedê re.
 
Health is good, thanks to God.

219
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Maşalla, tebîeta wî pirr xweş e.
 
Mashallah, his nature is very good.

220
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Welle ne baş im.
 
Well I am not good.

221
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Ne baş e, welle ne baş e.
 
He is not good, really not good.

222
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Welle ne baş im.
 
Well I am not good.

223
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Çima xalo?
 
Why uncle?

224
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Pêşiyê min diêşin, çokê min diêşin.
 
My back hurts, my knees hurt.

225
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Çokê te diêşin?
 
Your knees hurt?

226
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Heaa.
 
Yeah.

227
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Tu ji eşîra kê yî xalo?
 
Which tribe are you from uncle?

228
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Ez ji eşîra Brûkî me.
 
I am from the Bruki tribe.

229
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Brûkî?
 
Bruki?

230
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Brûkî.
 
Bruki.

231
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Gundê we çend mal in?
 
How many houses is your village?

232
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Gundê me, sê-çar mal mane.
 
Our village, three-four houses remain.

233
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Sê-çar mal?
 
Three-four houses?

234
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Eee.
 
Yes.

235
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Berê çiqas bûn?
 
How many were there before?

236
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Berê, şêst-heftê mal bûn.
 
Before, there were sixty-seventy houses.

237
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Şêst-heftê mal hebûn?
 
There were sixty-seventy houses?

238
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Eee, bar kirin çûn.
 
Yes, they migrated and went.

239
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Bar kirin.
 
They migrated.

240
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
Çûn bajara.
 
They went to the cities.

241
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Hemûyan bar kir?
 
Did they all migrate?

242
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Bar kirin.
 
They migrated.

243
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Kes nema.
 
No one remained.

244
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Hefs-heşt mal mane, ew jî xirab in.
 
Seven-eight houses remain, those are ruined too.

245
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Ereb in?
 
Arabs?

246
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Na na, ne ereb in.
 
No no, not Arabs.

247
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Min go qey tu dibê ereb in.
 
I thought you said they are Arabs.

248
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Na, xirab in xirab in.
 
No, ruined, ruined.

249
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Ha, xirab in.
 
Oh, ruined.

250
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Xirab in, xaniyên wan xirab in.
 
Ruined, their houses are ruined.

251
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
