306
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
No şikatê ben.. malê me.. malê me..
 
No, let there be complaints... our house... our house...

307
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,000
Şikatê xweber danî.. da biçin hecê wî.
 
He filed the complaint himself... so they could go to his
Hajj (pilgrimage).

308
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,000
Ne wî, vir malê me bî.
 
Not him, here was our house.

309
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Çû wî alî hecê wî, çû wî alî.
 
He went to that side for his Hajj, went to that side.

310
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,000
Malê me ew jêre.. malê jêre.. ev jêre.
 
Our house is that lower one... the lower house... this lower
one.

311
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:32,000
E temam xanîk ser hev ragirtine.
 
And okay, they built a house on top of each other.

312
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,000
Hewna.. xanî ed manin.
 
Those there... the houses remained.

313
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Te berda vî şikat.. gellek heye?
 
Did you drop this complaint... is there a lot [of evidence]?

314
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
Şikat têde heye.
 
There is a complaint in it.

315
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Û li bin da.. sê mal dikey têne.. ji buxarê têde nîne.
 
And underneath... three families fall into it... there is no
chimney in it.

316
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,000
Wala.
 
Really.

317
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Sê mal.. sê mal.. sê.. sê ev mal.. helek.. helek derekî hat
ketinê.
 
Three families... three families... three... three houses...
a group... a group from somewhere came and entered it.

318
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Yek.. doşekate dabeş kirine.
 
One... they divided the mattress/bedding.

319
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Şikat erê.. malê hûl yê?
 
The complaint yes... is the house rising up?

320
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Erê kuro.. malê hûl ye.. dereng hatin. Malê Xişmî çeqmeqane.
 
Yes boy... the house is rising... they came late. The House
of Xişmî is a clash/spark.

321
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
De îsan go ştewaye, kî noka çû.. belaw bûye.
 
Well, man said it is like this, who has gone now... it has
dispersed.

322
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:59,000
Her wextekê.. ştê ezm nake ser 'eysî.
 
Every time... things do not settle on life.

323
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Vêca qîçkê me gişk kuda çûne.
 
So, where have all our children gone?

324
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Qîçkê me herin çûne derkê.. dayîn..
 
Our children have all gone outside/away... given...

325
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Yekê çû Biftilîn.. çû Nevtilîn.. nebelîye.
 
One went to Biftilîn... went to Nevtilîn [place names or
metaphorical]... it is unknown.

326
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Tiştî belê tune erê.
 
There is nothing clear, yes.

327
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Yanî milet giş.. weno ev bîye.
 
Meaning the whole nation... it has become like this.

328
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Go tarîxana çêbîn bikin ser vê esasat, wana.. va ewa, destê
me.
 
If they make history on these foundations, them... look at
this, our hand.

329
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Ma bi kêfa xwe wadiyi? Ma bi kêfa xwe lê wira bîne?
 
Are we like this by our own choice? Are we here by our own
choice?

330
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Berê.. vê gundî.. baadînê hebûn, osne dikir..
 
Before... in this village... there were Badinis, they used
to do...

331
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Cîranê hev bûn, xêra me hebû.. biçûna baadînê xwe bi 'eşîra
hev.
 
They were neighbors, we had charity... if they went to their
Badini [areas] with their tribes.

332
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Ho.. va berê go tevir bî.. malê hewke bûn.
 
Oh... back when there was the axe... the houses were like
that.

333
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Çê.. kerîyê mezin hebûn.
 
What... there were large flocks.

334
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Malê vê.. Hemşîlê.
 
The house of this... Hemşîl.

335
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Nêrî.. çêkirinê.. şom û rûyî.. kes walo leyne hev bikin.
 
Look... the making... bad omen and face... no one brings
each other together like that anymore.

336
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,000
Noka.. çi, malê apê çî ye?
 
Now... what, what is the uncle's house [situation]?

337
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Ê.. êb xelq.. ê.. heqê xwe li ser hev tugre bikin.
 
Eh... eh people... eh... they impose their rights on each
other forcefully.

338
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
O.. wa giç.. canim feleh, ho begê çê?
 
Oh... that whole... my dear peasant, oh what about the Beg?

339
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:43,000
Malê we kî keca we.. û vî û diji?
 
Your house, who is your girl... and this and that?

340
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
Malê apê çî ye.. wane cînsî wane apê çî ye.
 
What is the uncle's house... them, their kind, what is the
uncle.

341
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Qanûn jî çûne, rawa heye noka.
 
The laws are gone too, there is opinion/custom now.

342
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:51,000
E nê nê.. li go avkê hêni dorbalîte hene.
 
Eh no no... according to the water cooler, there are
troubles.

343
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Dorbalîte.. cihek xopan e.. hene.. ez zanim.. xeberê vişê
heye.
 
Trouble... it's a ruined place... there are... I know...
there is news of the whisper.

344
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:58,000
Yanî.. amesa lon mêjin e.
 
Meaning... the sayings are old.

345
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:01,000
Bi gûne bopîlê me dane.. evna.. meselan.
 
By sin, our grandfather gave... these... stories.

346
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:07,000
Noka mezin, mezin hebe.. xêr bereket e. Noka merî mezin..
digerim, merî mezin kêm e.. wek kolne mezin.. emrê xwedê.
 
Now the elders, if there are elders... it is a blessing. Now
big people... I look around, old people are few... like old
pillars... God's age/will.

347
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:09,000
Kêm in.. yanî her gundekî dused katî bibîni.. tune bî.
 
They are few... meaning in every village if you see two
hundred times... they are gone.

348
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:11,000
Berê pir bûn.. cimaata xwe hebûn.. da we.
 
Before they were many... they had their gathering... gave
you.

349
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:15,000
Noka em vir xwedane.. ne dida bî, ne dîkê bî, ne rizma zik
ma heye hû..
 
Now we sit here... neither giving, nor sighting, nor is
there connection of the womb [kinship], oh...

350
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:19,000
Hev gûl xwdane.. ne dêka me tê, ne boka me tê, ne bopîrê me
tê.. haw çûn.
 
Giving each other flowers [sarcastic/metaphor]... neither
our mother comes, nor our father comes, nor our grandfather
comes... they have all gone.

351
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:23,000
Lê bû qişkino xêr gihaye.. çawa da çûn wan dûr.
 
But for the children, good has arrived... how they went far
away.

352
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Yanî wana em tê martê, dilê xwe de dizikînin.
 
Meaning they put us in trouble, they squeeze/hurt our
hearts.

353
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
Em bêhtir bar didin, navbê..
 
We give more burden, connection...

354
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Em ber xwedê digerin.. em sebira xwedê didin dilê xwe.
 
We seek God... we put God's patience in our hearts.

355
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,000
Em dibêjin wera bî.
 
We say let it be so.

356
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:37,000
Bare xelkê digû.. mela qîçkê mera hebin.. mera ne kurî coq
bin.
 
But people used to say... as long as we have our children...
let them not be cripples/useless to us.

357
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Xêr noka milet lê hebîne, kûrî coq bîne.
 
Good, now if the nation exists, let them be cripples
[sarcasm: better to be here and crippled than gone].

358
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,000
E rast e.
 
Eh, it is true.

359
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Em rûninke, xizmetê xwe bikin.. gî gerax.. kez.
 
Let us sit, do our service... all wondering... anyone.

360
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Walah wî ştew.. digîvşin.
 
By God, that... they are squeezing.

361
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Milet dûr ket.
 
The nation fell apart/far away.

362
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Bes berdestî mera hebe.. rind e.. mera.. mesela.. hûrik e..
em..
 
But if there is help at hand... it is good... for us... for
example... small... we...

363
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Law xwedê qusîrê ser me ke.. wa 'erebanê me wizingo yawa..
 
Oh son, God finds fault with us... those Arabs of ours like
that...

364
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:57,000
Dû wana ber pêlî kir.. amê bar vekewe.. amê çûyîne.
 
Following them, trampled... we will lift the load... we are
gone.

365
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:05,000
Min û kalo heta ser vê derecê.. bi çok û sêq.. heta ma rok
kir ber wê.. ez ber pê domam.
 
Me and the old man up to this degree... with knees and
legs... until the sun set before it... I continued on foot.

366
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:09,000
Wa pîşê xwe jî mesoha dikim.. ge tenok bi lingê mi da hav
bibe.. o.. hatim.
 
And I massage my front too... if a little heat gets into my
leg... oh... I came.

367
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,000
Te dikavê..
 
You fell...

368
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,000
Barê.. hew besin.. kobinê şikî ye.
 
Burden... that's enough... the knee is broken.

369
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:14,000
O sûrî çûyî.. o vînî?
 
Oh Syria is gone... oh do you see?

370
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:16,000
Ez silqşîm lingê xwe bidînim ser bilota.
 
I am sliding putting my leg on the tiles.

371
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:19,000
Mesele ne dereceyê.. belkê dinê çêkir.. ser..
 
The issue is not the degree... maybe the world made... on...

372
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,000
O sebir bîn.. bedî îngirîs li vir bû?
 
Oh be patient... were the English/British here eternal?

373
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:22,000
Lê?
 
Did you reach [that time]?

374
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,000
Lê?
 
What?

375
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Te.. heyştê, heyştê salî bî ma?
 
You... eighty, are you eighty years old?

376
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:28,000
Em li tû.. em hecî sê hecî li Tirkîyê.
 
We in... we Hajjis, three Hajjis in Turkey.

377
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:30,000
Ez noka.. el Tirkî jî uslum e.
 
I am now... Turkey is also Muslim.

378
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:33,000
Ereb û Tirk û Ecem û.. Kurd.. bira ne.
 
Arab and Turk and Persian and... Kurd... are brothers.

379
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,000
Eskerîm hat..
 
My soldier came...

380
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Ee.. em hatin.. gundî receb têbînim em.. ava reşo derebz mi
şef.. dekom ha sel girtin.
 
Ee... we came... I remember village of Receb we... that
black water railing my night... then Ha took the flooding.

381
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:42,000
No.. şêxû el girtin rehmetliq.
 
No... the Sheikh took the hand/people, may he rest in peace.

382
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Huseyn dêkom.. me jî Huseyn el girt.
 
Huseyn then... we also took Huseyn.

383
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Çîk mobînî ma du sal in e.
 
Just staying/waiting for us is two years.

384
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:57,000
Hew el girtin.. em dênava vêra bi şev.. bi 'ur'urê ga û
pês.. li kulê xistin peh derbas kirin.. hedî nedan.
 
They took/started... we were inside there at night... with
the roaring of oxen and dirty [conditions]... they put us in
the hut and kicked us through... they gave no rest.

385
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,000
Saeta te xweş.. bi sewrînîyorm.
 
May your hour be happy... I am delighted.

386
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Ha vaye madûm xêr.. ewêk.. yarebî..
 
Ha here is the lasting good... that one... Oh Lord...

387
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,000
Mişo û tevlok..
 
Mişo and Tevlok [Names/Nicknames]...

388
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,000
Hem tişta jî mawnî.. bigû..
 
And all things remained... say...

389
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Şta hawal jîro notin..
 
Things, friends did not come today...

390
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Em dînin.. bimborakî dikin, der dika.
 
We are crazy... we bless/congratulate, giving out.

391
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:13,000
O qîdal qîçkê gîha be.. xwedê mirazê dilê gîha bike.
 
Oh, may the children reach their goal... may God grant the
wish of everyone's heart.

392
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Xwedê poşmanîyê nede.
 
May God not give regret.

393
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Hacî miraz dil da xwedê bike.
 
Amen, amen.

394
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Hacî miraz dil da xwedê bike.
 
May God grant Haji the wish of his heart.

395
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:18,000
Amîn.
 
Amen.

396
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,000
U saeta te xweş.. saeta xalî min jî xweş.
 
And may your hour be happy... may my uncle's [husband's]
hour be happy too.

397
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Te jî xweş.
 
Yours too.

398
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,000
Saeta te jî xweş.
 
May your hour be happy too.

399
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:24,000
Saetkî pir xweş.. saetekî..
 
A very happy hour... an hour...

400
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Saeta te hebe..
 
May you have the hour...

401
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:29,000
Xwedê ca sogo hebîne.. beramberê xwa jî, ewî rasati rizqê we
tî daye.
 
May God keep you safe... opposite himself too, he has given
your provision truthfully.

402
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Kes nikê rizqê geşî bixwe.
 
No one can eat someone else's provision.

403
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:33,000
O reşî, o qelbone..
 
Oh blackness, oh fake/counterfeit...

404
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:34,000
Çi qirin çapo jine?
 
What dirt/filth of a woman is this?

405
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,000
E..
 
Eh...

406
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Me te dî, cemaat.. wekî wey dibên em..
 
We saw you, group/audience... as you say we...

407
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:40,000
Emê noka xatirê xwe ji wan bixwazin.
 
We will now ask their permission to leave.

408
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,000
Ê erê..
 
Eh yes...

409
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:43,000
Emke noka.. emê.. ber mal aren.
 
We now... we will... head towards home.

410
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Cem.. xalî min.. ew ebî.. Qelenq ebî.. lowik dergîstî
kirine.
 
At... my uncle's... he was... he was Qelenq... they got the
boy engaged.

411
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Xwedê xêrê wîne.. pşî gîyo.. qîçkê gîyo.
 
May God bring good... to everyone... to all children.

412
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,000
Xwedê destê xwe ser wera bigre.
 
May God hold his hand over them.

413
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Amîn, amîn keko.. xwedê serî te..
 
Amen, amen brother... God [bless] your head...

414
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:56,000
Saeta we jî xweş.. xwedê emrê kî dirêj bide.
 
May your hour be happy too... may God give long life.

415
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:57,000
Te jî..
 
You too...

416
00:26:57,000 --> 00:26:59,000
Kolê mezin hebin.. pîrê mezin hebin.. xêr û bereket ne.
 
If there are old pillars/men... if there are old women...
they are goodness and blessing.

417
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Merê mezin.. kefxweş dibe.
 
The old person... becomes happy.

418
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Rizqê mera bi rîtê.
 
Our provision is with the droppings [humble expression].

419
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:09,000
Dê.. bi merabe.. vîdokî hecer inşallah.. emê wera nîzik da..
emê vîdokî din Hecer wera teswîr kin.
 
So... stay with us... a video of Hecer God willing... we
will come to you soon... we will film another video of Hecer
for you.

420
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:14,000
Bîr nekin.. layk û îştîrak mera bidne.. û saeta we xweş.
 
Don't forget... give us a like and subscribe... and may your
hour be happy.

